/* Omega — the subobject classifier: what can be said of a proposition, three
 * values (Heyting G3), present, absent and unknown. Not a coproduct: its
 * three values are points of the carrier, not arms, and no match leaves it;
 * the one way out is `decide`, which lands in Decision, the coproduct of the
 * three answers. Its algebra is Heyting (prelude/alg/Heyting.yon), written
 * &&?, ||?, !?, =>?, with the laws of a Heyting algebra; the excluded middle
 * is no law of it (unknown ||? !? unknown is unknown).
 * Boolean, two points, enters it by the canonical injection, true to
 * present and false to absent; no arrow goes back. */
place Omega carried by proposition uses algebra Heyting {
}
